UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under AU-C 315.25, the auditor assesses the risk of material misstatement at two levels: the financial statement level (pervasive risks affecting many assertions) and the assertion level (specific risks for classes of transactions, account balances, and disclosures). Both levels are necessary for comprehensive risk assessment driving appropriate responses under AU-C 330.
Wrong (A): Assessing risk only at the financial statement level would miss specific assertion-level risks tied to individual accounts or transaction classes.
Wrong (B): Assessing risk only at the assertion level would miss pervasive financial-statement-level risks such as a weak control environment.
