-- Q1524: Risk Assessment [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under AU-C 240.32, management has the ability to override controls, and the auditor evaluates whether management''s business explanation for the override is reasonable and supported by evidence. If management provides a reasonable and corroborated business rationale, the auditor may accept the transaction after thorough evaluation.
Wrong (A): While evaluating the business rationale and assessing fraud risk are appropriate steps, this choice overstates the required response by treating every override as a definitive fraud indicator.
Wrong (B): Immediately reporting to law enforcement is not required; the auditor first evaluates the circumstances and considers the implications under AU-C 240.
Wrong (C): Ignoring the override is inappropriate because management override of controls is a recognized fraud risk factor under AU-C 240.A57 requiring evaluation.$EXPL$
