-- Q1532: Risk Assessment [hard/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under AU-C 240.A33, management providing overly optimistic revenue forecasts to support goodwill valuations involves manipulation of accounting estimates. While this could appear to be fraudulent reporting, management bias in estimates can also facilitate misappropriation through inflated asset valuations that mask diversions.
Wrong (A): An employee with sole custody of high-value inventory and no independent verification represents a classic misappropriation risk, but this is a more obvious scenario that typically involves physical asset theft.
Wrong (B): Selecting accounting policies to consistently maximize income represents fraudulent financial reporting through biased policy selection rather than asset misappropriation.
Wrong (C): Pressuring staff to capitalize expenses to meet earnings targets is fraudulent financial reporting through improper capitalization, not misappropriation of assets.$EXPL$
