-- Q1533: Internal Controls [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under AU-C 315.A60, the COSO Internal Control Integrated Framework identifies five interrelated components of internal control: control environment, risk assessment, control activities, information and communication, and monitoring activities. These components work together to provide reasonable assurance regarding an entity''s objectives.
Wrong (A): Five is the total number of COSO components, but the question asks about the framework''s component count as understood in the context of AU-C 315 auditing standards.
Wrong (B): Six exceeds the number of components identified by the COSO framework; there is no sixth component.
Wrong (C): Three would omit critical components; all five are required for an effective system of internal control under COSO.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1533;

-- Q1534: Internal Controls [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under AU-C 315.A60, the control environment is the foundation for all other components of internal control within the COSO framework. It sets the tone of the organization and includes factors such as management''s ethical values, philosophy, organizational structure, and human resource policies.
Wrong (A): Control activities are procedures that help ensure management directives are carried out, but they operate within and depend on the control environment rather than serving as the foundation.
Wrong (B): Risk assessment is the entity''s process for identifying and analyzing risks, not the foundational component of internal control.
Wrong (D): Monitoring activities evaluate whether controls are functioning over time but are not considered the foundation for all other COSO components.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1534;

