-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AU-C 315.A76, entity-level controls operate at a broad organizational level and have a pervasive effect on the entity''s internal control system. Examples include the control environment, entity-wide risk assessment processes, centralized monitoring activities, and the internal audit function, all affecting multiple processes and assertions.
Wrong (B): Controls operating at the transaction level within a specific account or business process are transaction-level controls, not entity-level controls.
Wrong (C): IT application controls are specific to individual systems and do not define entity-level controls, which encompass broader organizational elements.
