-- Q1541: Internal Controls [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under AU-C 315.14, the auditor''s evaluation of internal controls follows a two-step progression: first evaluating the design of the control (whether it is capable of preventing or detecting misstatements) and then determining whether the control has been implemented and placed in operation. AU-C 330.10 adds a third step of testing operating effectiveness if the auditor plans to rely on the control.
Wrong (A): Documentation in a policy manual relates to design evaluation, not to whether the control has been implemented and is actually operating.
Wrong (B): Testing by internal audit is a separate activity; the auditor''s assessment of implementation does not depend on internal audit having tested the control.
Wrong (C): Audit committee approval is not part of the auditor''s two-step evaluation of control design and implementation under AU-C 315.$EXPL$
