-- Q1551: Internal Controls [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under AU-C 315.A53, internal control provides only reasonable assurance due to inherent limitations including the possibility of collusion among employees to circumvent segregation of duties and management override of established controls. These limitations exist regardless of how well controls are designed and implemented.
Wrong (A): Controls apply to operations and compliance objectives as well, not only financial reporting; this does not explain the reasonable-versus-absolute assurance distinction.
Wrong (B): Small entities are not exempt from internal control requirements; size does not eliminate the need for controls under auditing standards.
