-- Q1560: Internal Controls [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under AU-C 330.A32-A33, automated controls perform consistently when properly designed and implemented because they are not subject to human variability. When IT general controls over program changes, access, and operations are effective and the automated control has not been modified, the auditor may reduce the extent of testing.
