Wrong (B): Retesting as a new control is unnecessary when the automated control is unchanged and ITGCs confirm no modifications have occurred since the prior period.
Wrong (C): Automated controls do not require the same sample sizes as manual controls because their consistent execution reduces the variability that larger samples address.$EXPL$
